# Test cases for rule 100010 (successful SSH login to 'student').
#
# Format, one case per line:   EXPECT|RULE_ID|LOG LINE
#   EXPECT = MATCH    the log line SHOULD make RULE_ID the final matching rule
#   EXPECT = NOMATCH  the log line should NOT trigger RULE_ID
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# ./test-rules.sh feeds each log line to the manager's wazuh-logtest and
# checks the outcome. Every rule you write should have at least one MATCH
# case and one NOMATCH case - a rule you've only tested with the "yes"
# case is a rule whose boundaries you don't actually know.

# A successful login as 'student' must fire our custom rule.
MATCH|100010|Jan  1 00:00:00 endpoint01 sshd[1234]: Accepted password for student from 10.10.10.20 port 54321 ssh2

# A successful login as any other account must NOT fire it (no false positive).
NOMATCH|100010|Jan  1 00:00:00 endpoint01 sshd[1235]: Accepted password for admin from 10.10.10.20 port 54322 ssh2

# A FAILED login as 'student' is a different event (rule 5760), not a
# successful one - our rule builds on 5715 (success), so it must not fire.
NOMATCH|100010|Jan  1 00:00:00 endpoint01 sshd[1236]: Failed password for student from 10.10.10.20 port 54323 ssh2
